test_stor_utm -- dump / stor at UTM coordinates (Nov 2026)
==========================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_stor_utm_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]          8 decks, about 2 s
  open summary.html

  REF_STOR=DIR sh run_stor_utm_tests.sh ...   also draw the volumes of
  another run (DIR = its work/ folder, e.g. a run with an older lagrit
  made with WORK=/tmp/old_work) in red in the pictures

WHAT IS TESTED

  Every deck writes one mesh twice: at the origin (files *_o) and moved
  to UTM-sized coordinates, + (7e5, 3.2e6, 1.5e3) (files *_u). The deck
  moves the mesh out and back before the first write, so both copies
  have the same geometry to the last bit (x - 7e5 is exact there); any
  difference between the two files is the writer's own loss of digits.

  same   the two files hold the same matrix (rows, columns) and the
         same volumes and coefficients, to 1e-12 of the largest value
  sum    the Voronoi volumes add up to the volume (2D: area) of the
         cells, computed by the checker from the mesh file (to 1e-9 of
         the sum of |Voronoi volume|)
  indep  the origin copy's volumes and coefficients agree (to 1e-7 of
         the largest; compression all merges values within 1e-8) with
         an independent computation in plain Python: for every edge of
         every cell, its piece of the Voronoi face (3D: the polygon
         edge midpoint - face circumcenter - cell circumcenter - other
         face circumcenter; 2D: edge midpoint to circumcenter), signed,
         gives the coefficient area / length and, as a pyramid over it
         (height half the edge), the volume of each end vertex

  st01  brick lattice 9 x 7 x 6 (1 x 0.75 x 0.5), interior vertices
        moved at random; dump / stor: the 3D default (anothermatbld3d.c,
        compression all)
  st02  st01's mesh; dump / stor / ... / ascii / scalar / graph
  st03  st01's mesh; dump / stor / ... / none and / coefs: the older 3D
        writer (matbld3d_stor.f); two coefs files in one run (the second
        was broken before Nov 2026: parking lot item 79)
  st04  random points on the faces of and inside a 1 x 1 x 0.5 box
        (make_stor_inputs.py); dump / stor / hybrid and without it
  st05  3D Poisson disk mesh, h = 0.08 in a 1 x 1 x 0.5 box (857
        vertices); dump / stor
  st06  2D: a 41 x 31 lattice in 0.04 x 0.03, interior vertices moved;
        dump / stor (matbld2d_stor.f)
  st07  st01's mesh; dump / pflotran: .uge volumes and areas (same), the
        centers u - shift = o to 1e-6 (the .uge has 13 digits)
  st08  file-name roots of 26 to 32 characters (the longest word LaGriT
        reads) for dump / stor (3D, 2D), pflotran, fehm and tecplot:
        every file gets its whole root and extension, and no file with a
        cut name is made (before Nov 2026 the name was built in 32
        characters: ROOT.s, or ROOT with no extension; item 76)

  KNOWN (reported, not a failure; parking lot item 80): on st04's mesh,
  whose hull has near-flat tets with far circumcenters, the 3D default
  writer's volumes add up to 0.5000006, not 0.5 (matbld3d_stor:
  0.500000000005), at the origin too. Shown as FIXED when it passes;
  then remove it from KNOWN in check_stor_utm.py.

  With LaGriT before Nov 2026 every deck fails (st08: 9 of its 13 files
  get cut names): the 3D default gave
  volume sums of -113.8 (st01) and 45.8 (st05) at UTM, with hundreds of
  negative volumes; matbld3d_stor lost about 1e-9 and 2D about 3e-7.

FILES

  run_stor_utm_tests.sh   runs the decks, then the checker
  make_stor_inputs.py     writes st04's vertex file into work/
  st*.lgi                 the LaGriT decks
  check_stor_utm.py       the checks, SVG pictures, summary.html
  work/, logs/            made by the run (not in git)
